    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38097" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeter-nāvĭgo</span></b> ,
			āre, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i>, <i>to sail by</i> or <i>past</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitans praeterpavigantium officia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 8, 3</span></i>.—With <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Baianum sinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Seyllam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. de Deo Socr. 24, p. 55, 30</span></i>
			.</div>
